11.100(a)","short":"Absence of Written Procedures","long":"There are no written procedures for production and process controls designed to assure that the drug products have the identity, strength, quality, and purity they purport or are represented to possess."},{"id":77,"cfr":"21 CFR 211.100(b)","short":"SOPs not followed / documented","long":"Written production and process control procedures are not followed in the execution of production and process control functions."},{"id":92,"cfr":"21 CFR 211.165(a)","short":"Testing and release for distribution","long":"Testing and release of drug product for distribution do not include appropriate laboratory determination of satisfactory conformance to the final specifications and identity and strength of each active ingredient prior to release."},{"id":12,"cfr":"21 CFR 211.170(b)","short":"Annual visual exams of drug products","long":"Reserve samples from representative sample lots or batches of drug products selected by acceptable statistical procedures are not examined visually at least once a year for evidence of deterioration."},{"id":93,"cfr":"21 CFR 211.170(b)","short":"Reserve samples identified, representative, stored","long":"Reserve drug product samples are not retained and stored under conditions consistent with product labeling."},{"id":109,"cfr":"21 CFR 211.188(b)","short":"Batch production and Batch Control Record Requirements","long":"The batch production and control records are deficient in that they do not include documentation of the accomplishment of each significant step in manufacturing."},{"id":17,"cfr":"21 CFR 211.192","short":"Investigations of discrepancies, failures","long":"There is a failure to thoroughly review any unexplained discrepancy whether or not the batch has been already distributed."},{"id":299,"cfr":"21 CFR 211.194(d)","short":"Laboratory equipment calibration records","long":"Laboratory records do not include complete records of the periodic calibration of laboratory instruments."}